    "intro": {
      "type": "od-text",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Oilily at OMARIEDEN",
        "heading": "Colour as a way of life",
        "text": "<p><em>Oilily has never done quiet. Since 1963 the Dutch label has dressed children, and later their mothers, in prints that clash on purpose, colours that refuse to fade into the background and a spirit of play that survives the school run. This season the collection lands at OMARIEDEN in full: tees and blouses, dresses, bottoms, knits, socks, bags and scarves, all made to be mixed, matched and worn with a grin.</em></p>",
        "align": "center",
        "width": "narrow",
        "size": "m",
        "button_label": "",
